{"id": "tech-4", "headline": "Hera probe images crater left by NASA DART impact", "source": "Ars Technica", "url": "https://arstechnica.com/space/2026/11/europes-hera-mission-returns-to-the-chaotic-scene-of-a-cosmic-smashup/", "published": "2026-11-25", "url_verified": true, "pages": ["The European Space Agency released the first views from its Hera spacecraft of the scar left by NASA's DART mission on the asteroid Dimorphos. DART struck the small asteroid in September 2022 at more than 13,700 mph, shortening its 12-hour orbit around larger companion Didymos by about 33 minutes. That was 25 times the most conservative expectation. Only distant telescopes and a small CubeSat saw the aftermath. Hera arrived near the pair after a two-year journey. Its images show the car-sized impactor carved a stadium-sized crater, nearly as large as Dimorphos, which is about 500 feet across. Scientists say the data should reveal what kind of mess DART made.", "The pair poses no risk to Earth, and was chosen because it resembles many near-Earth asteroids. Source: Ars Technica."], "qr": {"n": 41, "rows": ["11111110010111000101110100001111101111111", "10000010101101110100111001011100101000001", "10111010010111001110111100100011001011101", "10111010111110101000101101111100001011101", "10111010000111010010011100001011101011101", "10000010101110111110111010111010101000001", "11111110101010101010101010101010101111111", "00000000000000110010011010101000100000000", "11111011110001110100001111000110010101010", "00100101001010101011111111001011101111001", "11111010011010011010010000111000101000000", "00111100100010101000010010110000001011000", "00011010011110000011000011110111000001101", "11001101001000111000110101001111101111001", "11011010000111000011011001111100110110000", "00111001101100001001111110100011001011010", "10001011100111100111001001010100000100100", "11100101111111001111101111101111101110011", "00100010011001111100101000010000000110010", "11010001011111010110111010110001110011001